# Schedule map: P1 + P2 live

Owner: P1 (Ops) Marshal (f3810109-17a5-427f-9148-d58f645658e3). All times are Brisbane (AEST, UTC+10).
Phase status comes from /workspace/governance/phases.md, which is the source of truth. Updated 4 Oct 2026, 3:11pm.
Live: P1 (Marshal, Mender, Scorer, Safeguard, Safekeeper, Archivist, Architect, Explorer) and P2 since 4 Oct, 3:12pm (Scrutineer, Arbiter, Assembler, Inquirer, Inferer).
Dormant, with no scheduled work: P3 (Sourcer, Investigator, Interrogator), P4 (Mediator, Messenger, Imitator) and P5 (Emissary, Engineer, Extractor, Editor).
Retired 4 Oct: Moderator and Expediter (merged into Marshal), Meter (into Mediator), Minder and Maintainer (into Mender), Sentinel (into Safekeeper and Safeguard), Sanitizer, Surveyor, Ensembler and others.

## Daily chain (weekdays)

| Step | Bot | Starts on | Input | Output | Hands off to |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | P1 (Checks) Scorer | Own routine, weekdays 7:45am | Recent work from live bots | `/workspace/governance/assessments/YYYY-MM-DD.md` | P2 (Checks) Scrutineer, by priority message with the file path (from Mon 5 Oct) |
| 2 | P2 (Checks) Scrutineer | Scorer's handoff. Backup routine weekdays 11:45am skips if today's reviews exist, and tells the Marshal if the Scorer's file is missing | Today's dated assessment file | `/workspace/governance/reviews/YYYY-MM-DD.md` | P1 (Roles) Architect, by priority message with the file path |
| 3 | P1 (Roles) Architect | Scrutineer's handoff, not a clock time | Today's dated reviews file | Proposals, if any | Gem for approval (until P4 goes live, per R-004/R-005) |
| 4 | Gem | Architect's proposal | Proposal | Approval or rejection | P1 (Roles) Archivist |
| 5 | P1 (Roles) Archivist | Gem's approval or direct edit | Approved text | `/workspace/governance/codex/<bot>/vNNN.md` | None |

After P4 goes live, step 4 becomes P2 (Roles) Assembler for non-governance proposals. Governance-bot changes always go to Gem. P2 (Roles) Arbiter rules only on precedence conflicts and is not an approval step.
If a step's input file is missing, that step defers and doesn't run without it. The Marshal logs the deferral here and reports the stall to P1 (Ops) Mender.
A dated file is a signal to start work, not proof of who wrote it, because the computer is shared. Anything that looks wrong gets checked 1:1 with the claimed sender.

## Checks around the chain (weekdays)

| When | Bot | What |
|---|---|---|
| 10:20am | P1 (Ops) Marshal | Chain check: the Scorer's file and the Scrutineer's pickup. Logs deferrals and sends stalls to Mender |
| 10:50am | P1 (Ops) Mender | Stall and broken-handoff check, plus incident log |
| 11:45am | P2 (Checks) Scrutineer | Backup run (see step 2) |
| 1:15pm | P1 (Checks) Safeguard | Daily risk review and dry runs |

Note: the Marshal's 10:20am check comes before the Scrutineer's 11:45am backup, so it only flags a missing Scorer file or a handoff that hasn't been picked up yet. It doesn't treat unfinished reviews as a stall before 11:45am.

